# The build context of postgres.Dockerfile, the PostgreSQL image: an
# allowlist, which BuildKit reads in place of .dockerignore for that file.
#
# The first rule excludes everything; the rules after it let in exactly what
# the image is built from in the build context -- DB/fetch_verified.py, which
# downloads PostgreSQL's source and keeps it only when its SHA-256 is the one
# postgres.Dockerfile fixes, and DB/locked_files.py, which it imports, both
# mounted for that step without being copied; and the licence of the
# entrypoint scripts, third_party/docker-library-postgres/LICENSE, which the
# image carries. Nothing else of the checkout enters the image.
*
!DB/fetch_verified.py
!DB/locked_files.py
!third_party/docker-library-postgres/LICENSE
